The '''seventh series''' of ''[[The Great British Bake Off]]'' aired from 24 August 2016, with twelve contestants competing to be crowned the series 7 winner.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/tv/2016/07/11/the-great-british-bake-off-2016-everything-you-need-to-know/ |publisher=Telegraph |title=The Great British Bake Off 2016: everything you need to know – Olympics will delay new series |date=5 August 2016 |access-date=6 August 2016|newspaper=The Telegraph |last1=Hogan |first1=Michael }}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/news/the-great-british-bake-off-2016-start-date-bbc-one-show-delayed-thanks-to-the-rio-olympics-a7174311.html |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220618/https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/news/the-great-british-bake-off-2016-start-date-bbc-one-show-delayed-thanks-to-the-rio-olympics-a7174311.html |archive-date=18 June 2022 |url-access=subscription |url-status=live |date=5 August 2016 |work=The Independent |title=The Great British Bake Off 2016 start date: BBC One show delayed thanks to the Rio Olympics |access-date=6 August 2016}}</ref>

This series was the last to be broadcast on [[BBC One]], as the production company Love Productions opted to move the show to [[Channel 4]].<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/entertainment-arts-37353262 |title=Why did The Great British Bake Off move to Channel 4? |first= David |last=Sillito|date=13 September 2016 |work=BBC }}</ref> As such, it was also the last series to feature Sue Perkins, Mel Giedroyc, and Mary Berry.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/entertainment-arts-37355065 |title=Great British Bake Off: Mel and Sue to quit as hosts |date=19 September 2016 |work=BBC }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/entertainment-arts-37437907 |title=Great British Bake Off: Mary Berry leaves but Paul Hollywood stays |date=22 September 2016 |work=BBC }}</ref>

In the United States, the seventh series was broadcast as the fourth season on [[PBS]] and streamed as Collection 4 on [[Netflix]].

[[Sue Perkins]] does not appear in episode 2. When the episode was being filmed in April 2016 she needed time off to deal with a bereavement. She does appear vocally in the narration.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/newsbeat-37231057 |title=Sue Perkins will not appear in tonight's Great British Bake Off |date= 21 August 2016 |work= BBC }}</ref>

