=== Episode 7: Desserts ===
The Signature challenge required the bakers to make a family-sized [[swiss roll|roulade]] in {{frac|1|1|2}} hours. The judges were looking for a light sponge cake, even layers of filling, and a clean swirl. The technical challenge gave the bakes 3 hours to make a [[Dacquoise|marjolaine]], an unusual layered cake made with meringue, decorated with ganache and nuts. The showstopper challenge allocated 4 hours for the bakers to make 24 mini [[mousse]] cakes with 2 flavours (12 of each).<ref>{{cite news|last1=Newall|first1=Sally|title=The Great British Bake Off 2016 episode seven recap|url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/the-great-british-bake-off-2016-episode-seven-recap-dessert-week-a7347451.html |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220618/https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/the-great-british-bake-off-2016-episode-seven-recap-dessert-week-a7347451.html |archive-date=18 June 2022 |url-access=subscription |url-status=live|access-date=6 October 2016|work=The Independent|date=6 October 2016}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|last1=Hogan|first1=Michael|title=The Great British Bake Off: how a 'millennium wheel of lard' stole the show – plus the rest of the action from Dessert Week|url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/tv/2016/10/05/the-great-british-bake-off-how-a-triumphant-millennium-wheel-of/|access-date=6 October 2016|work=The Telegraph|date=6 October 2016}}</ref>{{sticky header}}{{table alignment}}
