=== Episode 8: Tudor (Quarterfinals) ===
Week eight featured the show's first [[Tudor period|Tudor]] theme, featuring food common in the 16th century. During the signature challenge, the 5 remaining bakers were asked to bake a shaped pie with Tudor flavours in 3 hours. The pie could be any type of pastry and they could use whichever fillings they wanted. In the technical, the contestants were asked to produce 12 [[Jumble (cookie)|jumbles]]—6 [[Monkey's fist|knot balls]] and 6 [[Triquetra|Celtic knots]]—in  {{frac|1|1|2}} hours. In the showstopper challenge, the contestants were asked to bake a marchpane ([[marzipan]]) cake in a [[three-dimensional space|three-dimensional]] shape in {{frac|3|1|2}} hours. However, all of the cakes had to be Tudor-themed.<ref>{{cite news|last1=Hogan|first1=Michael|title=The Great British Bake Off: Tudor Week proved to be unexpectedly tricky – with an even more unexpected ending|url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/tv/2016/10/12/the-great-british-bake-off-tudor-week-proved-to-be-unexpectedly/|access-date=13 October 2016|work=[[The Daily Telegraph]]|date=13 October 2016}}</ref>{{table alignment}}
