=== Episode 10: Royal Picnic (Final) ===
In the final signature challenge, the bakers had to make a filled meringue crown, which had to contain at least three layers of meringue, in 3 hours. In the technical, the judges decided to make a familiar bake challenging: the bakers had to make a Victoria sandwich, with no recipe or method given, in {{frac|1|1|2}} hours. The final showstopper involved the largest number of bakes ever requested in a challenge. The bakers were given 5 hours to make a picnic fit for the Queen, including 1 chocolate celebration cake, 12 sausage rolls, 12 mini [[quiche]]s, 12 savoury [[scones]] and 12 fruit and custard tarts.<ref>{{cite news|last1=Newall|first1=Sally|title=Our recap of The Great British Bake Off 2016 final|url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/the-great-british-bake-off-2016-final-recap-a7381311.html |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220618/https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/the-great-british-bake-off-2016-final-recap-a7381311.html |archive-date=18 June 2022 |url-access=subscription |url-status=live|access-date=28 October 2016|work=The Independent|date=26 October 2016}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|last1=Wollaston|first1=Sam|title=The Great British Bake Off final review – equal parts flour, butter, sugar, eggs and tears|url=https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2016/oct/27/great-british-bake-off-gbbo-final-flour-butter-sugar-eggs-tears|access-date=28 October 2016|work=The Guardian|date=27 October 2016}}</ref>
